Equivalence Groups Found
└── MQTT client for publishing telemetry over MQTT broker
    ├── Candidates : paho-mqtt, asyncio-mqtt, gmqtt
    ├── Used APIs  : mqtt.Client, client.connect, client.publish
    ├── Pitfalls   : paho-mqtt is synchronous and callback/thread-driven; asyncio-mqtt and gmqtt require an asyncio event loop and async/await syntax 
    │   throughout the calling code; Connection lifecycle differs: asyncio-mqtt uses 'async with Client(...) as client' context managers instead of explicit 
    │   connect()/disconnect(); publish() return values differ: paho returns a MQTTMessageInfo with .rc, async clients often return None or raise on failure 
    │   instead of exposing an rc code; The current code calls the MQTT client synchronously inside publish_reading/publish_batch, so migrating requires 
    │   converting these methods to async and updating all call sites; Dependency injection pattern (client=None -> _default_client) needs to be adapted for an
    │   async client factory (e.g., async context manager instead of eager construction)
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── paho-mqtt is used here as a synchronous, callback-based MQTT client to connect and publish telemetry readings. asyncio-mqtt (built on paho-mqtt but 
        exposing an async context-manager API) and gmqtt (a native asyncio MQTT client) serve the same functional role of publishing MQTT messages to a broker 
        and could substitute for paho-mqtt at the architectural level, though not as a drop-in without an async rewrite. amqtt is excluded as it is primarily 
        geared toward broker/server implementations rather than being a common client substitute in this pattern, though it could still serve a similar purpose
        if verified.

